Aim
To simulate a washing machine system using GPSS and analyze different stages of washing operations.

Theory
A Washing Machine System simulation represents the working process of washing clothes through different stages such as washing, rinsing, and spinning.
In this experiment, clothes arrive into the washing queue. Multiple washing machines act as servers. After washing is completed, clothes move to the rinsing stage and finally to the spinning stage.
The QUEUE block stores clothes waiting for processing. The SEIZE block assigns washing machines. The ADVANCE block represents processing time for each stage. The RELEASE block frees the machine after use.

Three stages used in the system:

Washing Stage
Rinsing Stage
Spinning Stage

This experiment helps in studying:

Multi-stage processing
Machine utilization
Queue management
Processing delays

Applications:

Laundry industries
Textile industries
Automated cleaning systems

Conclusion

Thus, the simulation of a washing machine system was successfully performed using GPSS. 
The experiment demonstrated multi-stage processing using multiple machines and helped in analyzing machine utilization and queue performance.
